<title>RUSSIA: Russian Q1 non-CIS oil, product exports rise yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian Q1 non-CIS oil, product exports rise yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian exports of crude oil outside the Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) in the first quarter of 1997 were 25.5 million tonnes (2.04 million barrels per day), which was eight percent more than a year earlier, the State Statistics Committee said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The committee said oil product exports in the first three months of the year jumped 43 percent year-on-year to 13.0 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The committee gave no breakdown for product exports, but provided the following data --  </p>
<p>RUSSIA NON-CIS JAN-MARCH 1997 ENERGY EXPORTS</p>
<p>		    (IN MILLION TONNES)</p>
<p>								  As pct of</p>
<p>				     Jan-March 1997     Jan-March 1996</p>
<p> Crude oil				25.5		    108</p>
<p> Products				 13.0		    143</p>
<p>Natural gas</p>
<p>  (billion cubic metres)	    33.9		    100</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
